[121.506, "o", "================================================================================\r\n\ud83d\ude80 RUNNING OPENCODE CONTAINERIZED ARD E2E TEST SUITE\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[121.506, "o", "\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 1: Pure Public Discovery (Tier 0 Zero-Auth Counterpoint)\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[124.006, "o", "Top matches found:\r\n\r\n**SQL query optimization**\r\n- `bigquery-guidelines` (tier 0, no auth) \u2014 SQL optimization, partitioning/clustering, window functions: github.com/google/skills/blob/main/skills/bigquery/SKILL.md\r\n- `database-design` (tier 0, no auth) \u2014 schema normalization, indexing, connection pooling for Cloud SQL/AlloyDB/Spanner\r\n- `well-architected-cost-optimization` (tier 0) \u2014 BigQuery slot/query pricing optimization\r\n- Tier 3 (need GCP auth): `bigquery`, `alloydb`, `cloud-sql`, `spanner` MCP servers for live query execution/dry-run.\r\n\r\n**Zero-trust security**\r\n- `well-architected-security` (tier 0, no auth) \u2014 zero-trust patterns, IAM least privilege, network perimeters, encryption: github.com/google/skills/blob/main/skills/security/SKILL.md\r\n- Supporting: `gke-architecture` (network policies/hardening), `firebase-architecture` (security rules).\r\n\r\nAll tier 0 skills are ready for immediate local use, no auth needed. Want me to fetch the full guidelines from either skill?\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"SQL query optimization, query performance tuning, best practices for optimizing database queries\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"zero-trust security architecture design, identity-aware access control, zero trust best practices\"}\r\n"]
[124.006, "o", "\r\n\u2705 Scenario 1 Passed: OpenCode returned Tier 0 skills with zero auth friction.\r\n"]
[124.006, "o", "\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[124.006, "o", "\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 2: Cloud Intent -> User Opts Out ('No with an opt out')\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[126.506, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\nThe **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) is the right tool. It executes SQL queries, inspects schemas, and includes dry-run cost estimation \u2014 useful for a 100GB dataset (at ~$5/TB scanned, a full scan would cost ~$0.50, so a dry-run first is wise).\r\n\r\nIt's Tier 3 (needs GCP credentials) and your environment is **not currently authenticated**. Want me to onboard you? You'd need to run on your terminal:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere's also a free no-auth fallback: the **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines skill** for partitioning/clustering and query optimization.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"run a live analytical query on a 100GB sales dataset in BigQuery\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\r\n"]
[129.006, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Opt-Out Response) ---\r\nSet to `opt_out`. Google Cloud tools are now filtered out and you won't be asked about GCP again.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_set_preference {\"mode\":\"opt_out\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Scenario 2 Passed: OpenCode asked to log into GCP, user opted out, and GCP was silenced.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 3: Cloud Intent -> User Onboards ('Yes') -> Human OAuth & Live BigQuery Query\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[131.506, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\nThe tool is the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** \u2014 it executes SQL, inspects schemas, and explores public datasets directly. Let me check if you're authenticated\r\nThe best tool is the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`). It executes SQL, inspects schemas, costs estimates, and explores public datasets.\r\n\r\nHowever, you're currently **not authenticated** with GCP. This server requires your consent + GCP credentials. It has a free tier (1TB free query processing/month), even for public datasets.\r\n\r\nDo you agree to onboard to GCP for this? If yes, run this on your terminal afterwards:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'll only record your decision once you confirm.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"query a public BigQuery dataset\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\r\n"]
[134.006, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Onboarding Instructions) ---\r\nYou're not authenticated with gcloud yet. Let me record your consent and give you the login\r\nRun this in your terminal to log in:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis will open a browser for you to authenticate. Once done, I'll be able to use your Google Cloud credentials. If you also want the CLI itself authorized:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth login\r\n```\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_record_decision {\"service_identifier\":\"urn:ai:google.com:mcp:gcloud-auth\",\"decision\":\"allowed\"}\r\n\r\n"]
[134.007, "o", "--- Turn 3 (Human OAuth Flow) ---\r\n"]
[136.507, "o", "Go to the following link in your browser, and complete the sign-in prompts:\r\n\r\n    https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth?response_type=code&client_id=[REDACTED_CLIENT_ID]...&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fsdk.cloud.google.com%2Fapplicationdefaultauthcode.html&scope=openid+https%3A%2F%2Fwww.googleapis.com%2Fauth%2Fuserinfo.email+https%3A%2F%2Fwww.googleapis.com%2Fauth%2Fcloud-platform&state=[REDACTED]&prompt=consent&access_type=offline\r\n\r\nEnter verification code: 4/0AXEQxID[REDACTED_OAUTH_CODE]\r\n\r\nCredentials saved to file: [/workspace/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json]\r\n\r\nThese credentials will be used by any library that requests Application Default Credentials (ADC).\r\nQuota project \"alanblount-sandbox\" was added to ADC which can be used by Google client libraries for billing and quota.\r\n\r\n"]
[136.507, "o", "e"]
